    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0440" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/3791: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="52" xml:id="d360-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1919-02-03T10:15:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1919-02-01T03:00:00+04:53"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 3, 1919, 10:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following from [Harris at] Omsk.</p>
                <p>“76. February 1, 3 a.m.</p>
                <p>On January 29th Kolchak took oath of office before the Senate in Omsk and
                    solemnly declared that the high power conferred upon him by the Council of
                    Ministers would be relinquished to the All-Russian Government which would be
                    created by a properly constituted constituent assembly. Harris.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d360-f1" n="52" type="source" xml:id="d360-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Commission to Negotiate Peace as Department’s no. 629, Feb. 8, 2
                    p.m.</p>
            </note>
